# APEX disk watchdog — see /opt/new-grype-scanner-v1/app/scripts/check-disk-usage.sh
#
# The platform has no deployed monitoring, so a silent scratch-dir leak took
# /opt from healthy to 97% full twice with nothing noticing until a human
# looked. Every 15 minutes is well inside the observed fill rate (~228 GB /46h,
# i.e. ~1.2 GB/min worst case) — slow enough to be free, fast enough to warn
# with hours of headroom.
#
# Alerting goes through logger(1) to syslog (tag: apex-disk-watchdog,
# daemon.warning / daemon.err). The log file below is for human triage only;
# cron mail is suppressed so a persistent WARN does not spam root.
SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
MAILTO=""

*/15 * * * * root /opt/new-grype-scanner-v1/app/scripts/check-disk-usage.sh >> /var/log/apex-disk-watchdog.log 2>&1
